This was the most annoying game I remember "playing".

The first half was fun.

But then the tedium kicked in: I was ready to ascend, except that I
had absolutely no way to harm Rodney. This weaponless, wishless, poly-
foo-less pacifist searched the entire dungeons (except the sanctum and
perhaps Ludios) but never found a ring of conflict, any potions of
gain level for pets, or other means to raise my level enough to farm
for an archon at the Castle level. The purple worm ate all the Valley
wraith, then died. After alchemy had left me with a very expensive
stack of booze but no gain level, I tried to pull the joker: I let two
tame liches grow up.

Unfortunately, they felt like teleporting into Rodney's chamber, but
not like fighting. So I had this mess on my hands: 1) an army of tame
gremlins that got in the way, 2) a master lich summoning monsters,
which I eventually pacified, 3) two Rodneys, carrying all the
invocation artifacts, 4) a few pets that were eating all the time and
would attack the troublemakers anyway, and 5) Yeenoghu.

Usually, getting a pet willing to attack Rodney is by far the hardest
part of the game. This time, it was horrible.


